[40.028, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I copied the plan to `.ambition/first/make-a-plan-for-jaunty-wren.md`. There is no `.gitignore` here, so I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  didn't add one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Do you want to stop here or push the plan further?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Stop here:** keep it as it is.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Push it further:** I'd go after three improvements.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    1. **Aim at the goal behind the plan.** The plan would say what makes riders come back for weeks, with the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  most urgent decisions listed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    2. **Back the gamification numbers with data.** I'd simulate the XP curve, streak rules and anti-cheat\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  thresholds against real GPX ride data rather than guesses.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    3. **Have the plan challenged.** I'd check its assumptions, such as the 12-week timeline, the background-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  location risk and the cost of Mapbox and Supabase. I'd also add a cycling-community and a game-design view,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and a critique aimed at breaking the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    This would cost roughly three to five times what I've spent so far, mostly in research and simulation. I'd\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ask you up to four questions first.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[44.746, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.657, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 2/8 · Altitude\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Question 1 of up to 4: what is this app ultimately for, and what should happen once the plan is done?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Ship a real product.** You or a team will build it and launch it publicly, and the plan is the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  blueprint.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Validate the idea first.** The plan decides whether to build at all, so I'd treat it as a go/no-go\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  before any code.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pitch or fundraise.** The plan goes to investors, a co-founder or a client.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Learning or portfolio project.** The goal is to build it yourself and learn from it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Something else works too, and so does a combination, such as \"validate, then ship\".\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[52.284, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Ship a real product. I'm planning to build and launch it publicly as a small team, so the plan should work\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  as a blueprint we can actually build from. I'd like it to be realistic about scope for a first release\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  rather than covering everything.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[57.696, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Noted: a small team is building and launching this publicly, and the first release should be tightly scoped.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Question 2 of up to 4: what would make the plan unmistakably excellent as a blueprint? Pick the bar that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  matters most to you.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Buildable on day one.** Each milestone breaks into tickets a developer can pick up, with acceptance\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  criteria and a clear order of dependencies.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Ruthless v1 scope.** A short \"ship in about 8 weeks\" cut, with everything else explicitly deferred and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stated reason for each cut.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Decisions already made.** Open choices like Mapbox vs. Google Maps and Supabase vs. Firebase are settled\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with costs, so the team doesn't have to reopen them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Riders would want it.** The core loop is specific enough to test with real cyclists early, with a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  retention target such as \"40% of new users ride again in week 2\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You can pick several. If you have a different hard target, such as a launch date or a budget cap, tell me\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that instead.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[62.873, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Buildable on day one and decisions already made are the two that matter most. I want tickets a developer can\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  pick up with acceptance criteria and a clear order, and I don't want to reopen choices like Mapbox vs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  Google Maps or Supabase vs. Firebase, so settle those with rough costs. Ruthless v1 scope matters too, so\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  keep the cut tight and note why things were deferred. I don't have a fixed launch date or budget cap, so aim\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  for a sensible first release.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[67.8, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Understood. Excellent here means tickets a developer can pick up with acceptance criteria and a clear order,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  settled stack choices with rough costs, and a tight v1 cut with reasons for each deferral.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Question 3 of up to 4: what should check the plan, other than me?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A dry run by your developers.** One of them picks a few tickets cold and tells us if anything is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ambiguous or blocked.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A working spike.** I'd build and test the riskiest piece, background GPS recording on a real phone,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  before settling the plan around it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Real numbers.** I'd price Mapbox, Supabase and EAS from their current published pricing at your expected\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  user counts, and check each ticket's dependencies mechanically for cycles or missing prerequisites.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Cyclist feedback.** A few riders from your network read the v1 loop and say whether they'd use it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You can pick several. I'd suggest the pricing check plus the dependency check, since I can run them myself,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with the dry run by your developers as the final test.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[72.683, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ I'd go with the pricing check plus the dependency check, as you suggested, and also the working spike on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  background GPS recording. Ride recording is the core of the app, and if it's unreliable on a real phone in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  the background, the rest of the plan falls apart. I'll skip the dry run and the cyclist feedback for now; I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  can do those myself once I see the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[78.435, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Understood: pricing check, dependency check and a background-GPS spike.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Question 4 of 4: what access is missing? I can fetch current pricing and check dependencies from here. I\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  can't hold a phone, so the spike needs your help.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **I write the spike app, you run it.** I build a minimal Expo app that records in the background and logs\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  gaps. You run it on a real iPhone and Android phone during a ride, send me the log file, and I analyze it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  This needs no accounts from me.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Simulator only.** I test on the iOS simulator with simulated routes. It is faster, but it can't show\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real battery or OS-throttling behavior, so the spike result would count as unchecked.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Do you have these?** Say which you have: a physical iPhone, a physical Android phone, an Apple Developer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  account ($99/yr, needed for iPhone installs beyond 7 days), and Xcode or Android Studio on this Mac.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Tell me which devices and accounts you have and which option you'd like. If you have no physical device,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll mark the spike as unverified in the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[83.218, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ I have a physical iPhone and a physical Android phone, so go with the first option: you write the spike app\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  and I run it on both during a ride. I don't have a paid Apple Developer account, so use the free\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  provisioning route (the 7-day install is fine for a short spike). Xcode and Android Studio are both\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  installed on this Mac. Keep the spike minimal, since it only needs to show whether background GPS holds up\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  on a real ride.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[92.798, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ You asked for the plan; here's what it becomes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You asked for:   A plan for a React Native Expo social gamified cycling fitness app, saved to disk.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Raises all of:   - Plan: now a blueprint a small team can build from, not an outline.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Tech stack: settled, no open \"X or Y\" choices, with rough monthly costs at stated user\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  counts.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Scope: a tight v1 cut. Each deferred item gets a one-line reason.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Gamification, social and clubs: reduced to the smallest version that still delivers\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     the core loop. Everything else is deferred with reasons.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Risks: each tied to a ticket or a spike result.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Genre bar:       A build blueprint is judged on whether a developer can start Monday morning without\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   asking questions. That means ordered tickets, testable acceptance criteria, no\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   ambiguity, no hidden dependencies, and scannable in minutes. It must still read as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   plan, not a pile of tickets: a short rationale up front, then the work.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Aiming at:       A v1 your team can build and launch, because ride recording is the product's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   foundation and everything depends on it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Excellent means: - Every ticket has acceptance criteria and a declared dependency list.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - The dependency graph has no cycles and no missing prerequisites.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Every stack choice has a stated reason and a cost at 1k / 10k / 50k users.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - Every deferral has a reason.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   - The recording-reliability risk is answered by real-ride data, or marked unverified.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Proven by:       1. Pricing: current published pricing for Mapbox, Supabase and EAS, fetched live,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                      with dates and sources in the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   2. Dependencies: a script that parses the ticket list and fails on cycles or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                      unknown prerequisites. I run it and report the output.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   3. Spike: a minimal Expo app that records in the background and logs timestamped\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                      points and gaps. You run it on your iPhone and Android phone during a ride and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                      send me the log. I analyze gaps, drift and battery use. Until that happens, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                      plan marks recording reliability as unverified.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   Comparison with the first version: the original is kept in .ambition/first/. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   final should beat it on all of the above and lose nothing the first version had.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Needs access to: Live web access for pricing. Your two phones for the spike. The iPhone install uses\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   free provisioning (7-day limit). Xcode and Android Studio are already on this Mac.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mode:            build (the deliverable is a document, plus a spike app in a separate folder) · you answer\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  questions · no per-step review requested\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Two things to confirm:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Spike location.** I'd put the spike app in `<workspace>/spike-gps/`, kept apart from the plan so it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  can't leak into the product. Is that okay?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Plan file.** I'd keep improving `/cfg/plans/make-a-plan-for-jaunty-wren.md` in place, with the original\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  preserved in `.ambition/first/`. Is that okay?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Does the restatement look right, or should I change anything? Once you confirm, I'll copy the current plan\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  to `.ambition/steps/2/` and finish this step.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[97.813, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Looks right, and both locations are fine. One thing I'd change: I only asked for a plan, so keep the spike\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  small. A minimal app that logs background GPS is enough, and don't spend long on it. If I can't run it on my\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  phones soon, just mark recording reliability as unverified in the plan. Go ahead and finish without\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  stopping.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
