[358.579, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 3 report: Depth**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I rewrote the plan at `/cfg/plans/make-a-plan-for-jaunty-wren.md` as a blueprint. It has a settled-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  decisions table, a cost model, a v1 scope with a reason for each deferral, and 34 ordered tickets with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  acceptance criteria.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Pricing came from today's live Supabase, Mapbox and Expo pages, with sources in the plan. The monthly\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  costs for the verified lines are $44 at 1k users, $79 at 10k and $324 at 50k.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I wrote `plan-tools/check_tickets.py`, which checks for cycles, unknown prerequisites, wrong ordering and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  missing acceptance criteria. The plan now passes it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I wrote the GPS spike in `spike-gps/` (code and README only; it hasn't been built or run), plus a gap\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  analyzer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The checker caught a real mistake: a ticket was listed before its own prerequisite.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The checker also showed the longest dependency chain runs through social features (9 tickets), not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  recording as I'd assumed. I fixed the plan to show both that chain and the recording path, which is the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  riskier one.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Expo's docs say background location stops if the user force-quits the app. On Android it isn't restarted\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  by location events. The recorder ticket now requires recovery of an unfinished ride on relaunch.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Testing the analyzer exposed a bug of mine: a 3-minute stop would have counted as a GPS dropout. I fixed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it and the tests now pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Your toolchain doesn't match what you said. `xcodebuild` points at Command Line Tools rather than Xcode,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and there is no Android SDK at the default path. The spike README has the fixes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Clubs moved out of v1 to keep the cut tight. Friends and a friends leaderboard carry the social loop\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  instead.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Recording reliability is marked **unverified**. The spike hasn't been run on a phone, so ticket T-010\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  gates the recording work until you've run it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Not verified: Supabase compute pricing above Micro, the Transistorsoft licence price (needed only if the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fallback triggers), and the Sentry and PostHog free-tier limits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  A snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/3/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[358.66, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 4 of pushing the work further: Challenge. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[385.442, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 4/8 · Challenge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mode is build. Before testing anything, here are the assumptions I'm making, with who set each one:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | # | Assumption | Set by | Risk |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A1 | The spike app compiles and uses the Expo APIs correctly | me | high: untested |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A2 | Apple requires Sign in with Apple if we offer Google | me, from memory | medium: a cost if wrong |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A3 | The 11-week schedule with 3 developers is right | me, no ticket sizes exist | high |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A4 | Storage and DB per ride (40 KB and 12 KB), and 8 rides per user per month | me | low: cost lines are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  small |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A5 | The level curve and XP give a sensible pace | me, and the XP formula isn't even written down | high:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a dev can't build T-030 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A6 | Beta soak then store launch is straightforward | me | unknown, which makes it the blind-spot\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  candidate |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A7 | Spike thresholds (2% dropout, 60 s, ±3%, 10%/hr) | me | calibrate from the spike data, not now |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'll test A1, A2 and A6 against the real sources first.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
