[539.086, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 4 report: Challenge**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did.** I tested the plan's assumptions against the real sources and fixed what failed. The plan checker\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (now 35 tickets) and the analyzer test both pass after the fixes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Assumption | How I tested it | Result |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | The spike app compiles and uses Expo correctly | Installed the real packages (Expo SDK 58) and ran `tsc`;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  read the location plugin and Android manifest | **Failed, then fixed.** The task executor had to be async.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The plugin keys and the `location` foreground-service type exist. Typecheck is clean, but the app is still\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  not built or run on a device. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Apple requires Sign in with Apple when Google is offered | Read guideline 4.8 | **Wrong reason.** It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  requires an equivalent privacy-preserving login, not Apple specifically. The decision stays, with the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rationale corrected. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 11 weeks with 3 developers | Sized all tickets (126 dev-days) and computed bounds with the checker |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Mostly holds:** about 12 weeks at 70% focus. With 2 developers it is about 18 weeks. The sizes are still\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  my estimates. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 40 KB and 12 KB stored per ride | Measured a synthetic one-hour ride | Raw track is 39 KB gzipped, which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  matches. The DB figure was too high (about 3 KB). Real tracks will be noisier. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Level curve and XP | Simulated four rider types over 52 weeks | **Failed.** The plan had no XP formula, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  keen rider reached level 167, and a commuter's first ride didn't reach level 2. I replaced it with a steeper\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  curve and a weekly soft cap, which gives levels 12 to 46 at one year. The rider types are invented, so this\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is a starting point. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **New finding.** Google Play requires a closed test with at least 12 testers opted in for 14 straight days\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  before a new personal account gets production access. My schedule never mentioned it. I added ticket T-007\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (accounts and recruiting 12 Android testers) and made the beta soak double as that test. Google's page\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  didn't say whether organization accounts are exempt, so that is flagged to check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changed course.** The pacing numbers and the 8-rides-per-user-per-month figure remain assumptions, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  plan labels them that way. The 2% / 60 s / ±3% / 10% per hour spike thresholds are still untested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  A snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/4/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
