[573.562, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mode is build. In verbs, the plan has to help a small team do five things:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Decide** the stack, scope and order of work, and **estimate** it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Record** a ride reliably.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reward** riders so they come back without pushing them to ride harder or riskier.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Share** rides so friends can see and cheer each other.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Protect** where riders live.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The first two are the genre's own verbs: a blueprint decides, orders and estimates, and the app must record.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  These are the fields I'm borrowing from:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Lead mobile engineer (the genre's best practitioner).** Method: build a thin working slice end to end\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  first, then widen it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Behavioural game designer.** Method: simulate whether a reward loop works for every kind of rider before\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  committing to it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Road-safety human-factors engineer (the field I wouldn't normally consider).** Method: hazard analysis\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  of the incentives themselves. Which rewards make a rider go faster, take risks or look at a screen while\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  moving?\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Privacy and OSINT attacker (the red team).** Method: attack the privacy zone with the data it actually\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  publishes, and look for who could be harmed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Two things can be tested now: the privacy-zone attack and the quest-fairness claim. I'll also check Apple's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rules for user-generated content.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
