[876.825, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 6 report: Judge**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did.** I built `plan-tools/plan_lint.py`, an outside check that holds the plan to its promises. It\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  recomputes the plan's numbers from code and sources: costs, schedule, XP examples, quest and privacy\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  figures. It also resolves every cross-reference, checks the original ask and each restatement promise, and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  checks that each principle has a ticket enforcing it. The plan passes 40 of 40 checks. The same check gives\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the first version 9 of 36. I also gave the plan a full cold read, and a snapshot is in `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the checks showed.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Mutation controls:** six deliberate breakages (a cost, an XP example, a level, a dangling reference, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  dependency cycle, a principle) each tripped the lint, so it can fail. My first cycle attempt used a `sed`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  form that doesn't work on macOS; the portable version failed correctly.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Lint bugs:** two of my first three failures were parsing mistakes in the lint (an indented table, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  persona name with parentheses), not plan faults. I fixed the lint.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Plan faults from the cold read, now fixed:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Streak bonus:** the text said max +20% but the tested simulation used +25%. XP is now defined once, in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `plan-tools/sims/xp_rules.py`, which generates the plan's worked examples. This moved the commuter's year-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  end level from L24 to L23.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Missing details:** the eight badges were promised but never listed, and the five worked XP examples were\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  missing. Both are now in the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Dependence on throwaway files:** the plan pointed at scripts in `.ambition/`. They're now in `plan-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tools/sims/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Contradictions and gaps:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Dated week labels contradicted the computed schedule.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Section 3 said to start the Play review early but pointed at a late ticket.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The v1 scope list omitted follow approval and block/report.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - \"XP can't be forged\" overclaimed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A stale \"earlier MVP\" mention referred to a version your team never saw.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - No ticket measured the 40% second-ride target.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Things the first version had and I'd dropped:** target users, end-to-end tests (now T-019), and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  launch-region question. I also added km/miles units, which neither version had.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Usability:** the plan grew from 97 to 398 lines. To keep it scannable I added an \"At a glance\" block at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the top with the numbers, the biggest risk and the first three actions, and the lint checks those numbers\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  against the real ones.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Now vs. first version.** The plan is better on every part of the ask and on the goal, and I found nothing\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it does worse. The first version is shorter and easier to skim, but it couldn't be built from. It is 13\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  weeks for 3 developers with 37 tickets and 133 dev-days.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Still unchecked.** A cold read by your developers (you said you'd do that) and the real-phone spike. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sizes and thresholds are still my estimates.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
