[949.394, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mode is build. The plan's current target is the full v1 in about 13 weeks with 3 developers. The stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  target is **12 riders recording real rides with XP on their own phones by the end of week 4 (3× faster), and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a public store launch by week 8 (1.6× faster)**. The current plan stays as the fallback.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  To see if that holds, I'll write a tool that takes a sub-release (which tickets are in, which are shrunk,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  which dependencies are cut) and computes what it costs. First, one thing I noticed while sizing. T-010 (the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  GPS spike) says it depends on T-002 (EAS builds), but the spike app builds locally with no EAS. That\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  dependency is false, and it delays the riskiest check in the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
