[1060.024, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ **Step 7 report: Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Did.** I raised the plan's target and kept the 13-week full v1 as the fallback. The stretch is 12 riders\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  recording real rides with XP by the end of week 4 (3× faster), and a public store launch by week 8. The plan\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  gets there by shipping two earlier releases. I wrote `plan-tools/releases.py`, which computes each release's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  effort and schedule and fails if a release includes a ticket whose prerequisite is missing. The plan now\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  passes all 49 lint checks, and I snapshotted it to `.ambition/steps/7/`. The full-v1 tickets are unchanged.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the numbers say (70% focus):**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Release | 3 developers | 4 developers |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | S1: first riders | 5.0 weeks | **4.0 weeks** |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | S2: public launch | 11.0 weeks | 8.3 weeks |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | S2 without kudos and the friends leaderboard | 10.6 weeks | 7.9 weeks |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Full v1 (the fallback) | 12.7 weeks | 10.3 weeks |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Found.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The first attempt missed.** It gave 4.6–4.9 weeks for S1, held back by the recording path. Three changes\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fixed that: starting the geo library on day 1 before the app skeleton exists, building the record screen\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  against a mocked recorder while the background task is written, and running the GPS spike on day 1.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A false dependency:** T-010 depended on T-002, but the spike builds locally, so the dependency delayed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the riskiest check for no reason. I removed it from the full plan too, and fixed the stale \"riskiest path\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sentence that had relied on it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it breaks.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **S1 hits 4.0 weeks with zero margin, and only with 4 developers.** Each day lost on the critical path\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  costs about 1.4 calendar days.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **If recording takes twice as long** (for example if the spike fails), S1 lands at 6.0 weeks whatever the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  team size.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **S2 misses 8 weeks by 0.3 weeks.** It fits only by dropping kudos and the friends leaderboard, which\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  weakens the \"compare with friends\" loop. It also has no push notifications, so no streak reminder, which may\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hurt the 40% second-ride target.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not in the numbers:** your two spike rides in week 1, a paid Apple account on day 1 (free provisioning\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  can't reach testers' iPhones), and store review waits. Starting the parallel work early could also cause\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rework.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
