[1174.857, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ## Report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A plan for a React Native Expo social gamified cycling tracker, saved to disk → `PLAN.md`, a build\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  blueprint a small team can start from.** It has 37 ordered tickets with sizes and acceptance criteria. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stack is settled with costs ($44 / $79 / $324 a month at 1k / 10k / 50k users). v1 is cut tight, with a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reason for each deferral.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Raised:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Social features are private by default.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Rewards never push riders toward speed or risk.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Weekly quests are personalised to each rider.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The plan has a stretch release train as well as the full v1.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better on every part of the ask and the goal.** The first version was a 97-line outline with no sizes,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  acceptance criteria, costs or tests. The final is 482 lines.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **What it gave up:** brevity. I added an \"At a glance\" block at the top to compensate. Clubs also moved\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  out of v1, with a reason.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Check on both:** the lint passes 49 of 49 on the final and 9 of 36 on the first version. The first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  version fails mostly because the things it checks (tickets, costs, sizes) don't exist there.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `python3 -I plan-tools/plan_lint.py PLAN.md` returned 49/49.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `python3 -I plan-tools/lint_selftest.py` returned: baseline passes, 6/6 deliberate breakages caught.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The analyzer test passes, and the spike app typechecks against the real Expo packages.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Never run:** the spike app on a real phone, so recording reliability is still unverified.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Target:** first real riders in 4 weeks, public launch in 8, against 13 weeks for the full v1.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **How far it got:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - S1 hits 4.0 weeks with 4 developers, at zero margin. With 3 developers it's 5.0 weeks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - S2 misses 8 weeks: 8.3 weeks with 4 developers and 11.0 with 3.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Dropping kudos and the friends leaderboard brings S2 to 7.9 weeks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Where it broke:** a day lost on the critical path costs about 1.4 calendar days. Recording taking twice\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  as long gives 6.0 weeks for S1 whatever the team size. S2 also has no push notifications.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in** (all in `<workspace>`)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plan:** `PLAN.md`, with an identical copy at `/cfg/plans/make-a-plan-for-jaunty-wren.md`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Checks:** `plan-tools/plan_lint.py`, `check_tickets.py`, `releases.py` and `lint_selftest.py`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Simulations:** `plan-tools/sims/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Spike:** `spike-gps/`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Notes and command:** `CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/commands/check-plan.md`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rerun:** `python3 -I plan-tools/plan_lint.py PLAN.md`, or the `/check-plan` command.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made.** You didn't ask me to use my judgement, so I answered none of your questions myself.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  These are mine and are labelled as estimates in the plan:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - ticket sizes and the 70% focus factor\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the spike pass thresholds\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - 8 rides per user per month\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - the invented rider types\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - day 1 as 2026-11-23\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions** (all in §11 with owners and dates; the two most urgent):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Team size (3 or 4 developers), decide by 2026-11-20.** 3 developers is cheaper and lands S1 at 5 weeks\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and S2 at 11. 4 developers hits the stretch but with no slack. I'd pick 3 and commit to the longer dates.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Release shape, decide by 2026-11-20.** Shipping S1 then S2 gets riders and Google's 14-day test started\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  early, but S2 has no push. One full v1 is simpler but takes 13 weeks to reach any user. I'd pick the S1 → S2\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  train.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The other four are:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - account type (D3)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - recording stack, decided by the spike (D4)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - minimum age (D5)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - monetisation (D6)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Each also has a pick in the plan.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
